      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greentown%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village borders the Ledgedale Recreational Area and includes shoreline on Lake Wallenpaupack.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greentown%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Peggy Bancroft Hall, home of the Greene‑Dreher Historical Society, stages events like the 1776 – The Musical celebrating Independence Day.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.greenedreherhs.org/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 2025 the Historical Society marked the 70th anniversary of the 1955 flood that reshaped the local landscape.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.greenedreherhs.org/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "June 6, 2026, the Society will host a Plant Sale Fundraiser at Carlton Drake Park, inviting garden lovers to buy perennials.",
